+# Final review inv-2, cluster 28 (src-plan)
+
+Source: base 60e287aadd08af10779df39e625200f28d4b7fa3, head 985d1eb6faaa2e92e4e01f430f0f2c07618bf6ad (both verified with `git rev-parse --verify <sha>^{commit}`). Caller checkout HEAD observed at 985d1eb6, status clean. Inputs: slices/000147.diff (src/plan/seat_adopt.rs) and slices/000148.diff (src/plan/tests.rs), digest.md for context, epic hg-lnw and its design doc `docs/superpowers/runs/2026-11-26-resurrect-seat-frictionless-restart/2026-11-26-resurrect-seat-frictionless-restart-design.md`.
+
+## What the cluster changes
+
+- `src/plan/seat_adopt.rs`: the adoption plan's keyless warning changes from "closing its tab and undoing that gives the pane a fresh threads seat" to the windowed wording: undo within 7 days brings back the threads seat, everything within 24 h, receipts and ordinary invitations settled after that, fresh seat and loss of memberships graph does not own after 7 days. The unit test `seat_adopt_prints_the_g5_warnings` is updated to the same string.
+- `src/plan/tests.rs`: `restore_commit_clears_occupant_and_runtime` builds `SeatFactState::Retired` with the two new fields (`keyed: true`, `retired_at: None`), a mechanical follow-on of the enum change in `src/model/clone.rs` (commit 98a6afd). The test's subject (restore commit clears occupant and runtime) does not depend on keyed or retired_at, and `reversible: false` keeps it on the final path.
+
+## Spec trace
+
+- Design section 3 requires: "The adoption plan warning (`src/plan/seat_adopt.rs`) changes from 'closing loses the seat' to the windowed wording." Delivered. The text matches the windows in section 3 (24 h, 7 d, final) and README "Keyless seats" at head.
+- Requirement baseline B1 (resurrect the closed tab's seat on undo): this cluster carries only the user-facing plan text; the behavior lives in the threads/reconcile/undo clusters and is the seam reviewer's to trace from `herdr-graph undo`. The warning promises what the design and README promise, so no over-claim is introduced here.
+- B2, B3, B4: not touched by this cluster (restart rebind, pin, U2 live elsewhere).
+- Test evidence at head: `plan::seat_adopt::tests::seat_adopt_prints_the_g5_warnings ... ok` and `plan::tests::restore_commit_clears_occupant_and_runtime ... ok` in evidence/hg-lnw.24/rebased-lib.log and evidence/hg-lnw.25/cargo-test-lib.log. Neither file changed after those runs (last touching commit 8fc8386, before them).
+
+## Wording notes
+
+- The 24 h to 7 d clause says ordinary invitations owed to the seat "are settled" but not that graph re-issues its own seat-wide invitations (design section 3 invitation reset; README says so). An operator reading only the plan may expect to re-invite graph's channels by hand. Minor; README covers it.
+- The warning does not mention that `clone purge` of a closed keyless clone finalizes the seat at once, ending the 7-day window (design section 3, README). Operator-explicit action, documented in README; acceptable to omit from the adopt plan.
+
